    "path": "Angular/Angular-Detailed-Chunk-02-Components-Lifecycle/README.md",
    "content": "# Angular Interview Guide — Chunk 2: Components and Lifecycle\n\n- [11. How Do Parent and Child Components Communicate?](011-parent-child-component-communication.md)\n- [12. How Do You Avoid Putting Too Much Logic in a Component?](012-avoid-too-much-component-logic.md)\n- [13. How Do You Design Reusable Angular Components?](013-design-reusable-components.md)\n- [14. How Do You Pass Data Between Unrelated Components?](014-unrelated-component-communication.md)\n- [15. What Are @Input and @Output?](015-input-and-output.md)\n- [16. What Are Angular Lifecycle Hooks?](016-angular-lifecycle-hooks.md)\n- [17. What Is EventEmitter?](017-eventemitter.md)\n- [18. Constructor vs ngOnInit in Angular](018-constructor-vs-ngoninit.md)\n- [19. When Do You Use ngOnDestroy?](019-when-to-use-ngondestroy.md)\n- [20. When Do You Use ngOnInit?](020-when-to-use-ngoninit.md)\n"
