    "content": "# Angular Interview Guide — Chunk 12\n\n## Angular 22 Deep Dive — Part 1\n\n- [116. How Do resource and httpResource Model Asynchronous Signal-Based Data?](116-resource-and-httpresource.md)\n- [117. How Do You Implement Synchronous, Asynchronous, Cross-Field, and HTTP Validation with Signal Forms?](117-signal-forms-validation.md)\n- [118. What Security Responsibilities Belong to Interceptors and Route Guards, and What Must Always Be Enforced by the Backend?](118-interceptor-guard-backend-security.md)\n- [119. Which Angular 22 Features Would You Adopt Immediately, and Which Would You Introduce Incrementally?](119-angular22-adoption-strategy.md)\n- [120. Design an Angular 22 Screen That Loads a Large Dataset, Supports Filtering, Preserves URL State, and Remains Fast and Accessible](120-large-dataset-screen-design.md)\n- [121. How Do Loading, Value, Error, Refresh, and Cancellation Behave in a Signal-Based Resource?](121-resource-lifecycle.md)\n- [122. How Do OnPush, Signals, and Zoneless Change Detection Work Together?](122-onpush-signals-zoneless.md)\n- [123. How Do Route-Level Server, Prerender, and Client Render Modes Work in a Hybrid Angular 22 Application?](123-hybrid-route-render-modes.md)\n- [124. How Do Signal Forms Differ from Classic Reactive Forms, and How Would You Migrate a Large Form Gradually?](124-signal-forms-migration.md)\n- [125. How Do signal, computed, linkedSignal, and effect Differ, and What Is an Appropriate Use Case for Each?](125-signal-computed-linkedsignal-effect.md)\n\nEach question is in a separate detailed Markdown file.\n"
