    "path": "Angular/Angular-Detailed-Chunk-14-Angular14-to-22-Migration-Part1/README.md",
    "content": "# Angular Interview Guide — Chunk 14\n\n## Angular 14 to Angular 22 Migration — Part 1\n\n- [136. How Would You Roll Out Angular 22 Safely and Recover if Production Metrics Regress?](136-safe-rollout-and-recovery.md)\n- [137. What Build, Bundle-Size, Performance, SSR, Accessibility, and Browser-Regression Checks Would You Run Before Release?](137-pre-release-quality-checks.md)\n- [138. After Reaching Angular 22, How Would You Prioritize Optional Modernization and Measure Whether It Creates Value?](138-prioritize-modernization-value.md)\n- [139. How Would You Migrate Constructor Injection to inject and Decorator Inputs to Signal Inputs Without Destabilizing the App?](139-migrate-inject-and-signal-inputs.md)\n- [140. How Would You Migrate Karma Tests to Vitest and Identify Behavior Hidden by Brittle Tests?](140-karma-to-vitest-migration.md)\n- [141. How Would You Migrate NgModules to Standalone APIs Incrementally?](141-incremental-ngmodule-to-standalone.md)\n\nEvery question is contained in a separate detailed Markdown file.\n"
